                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "16854157",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198009165686",
                            "num_reviews": 4,
                            "playtime_forever": 158,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 116,
                            "last_played": 1478574408
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I really want people to play this game! It's a cute idea that seems like a blast to play with friends. However, the game needs more people playing it. If you're on the fence about buying it, here is what you should know:\n\nPros:\n-Cheap! Game is a steal honestly. Its not at its peak value yet because of the small playerbase, but it's a tiny investment.\n-Simple concept. Gets the job done with streamlined gameplay that really gets to the core of class based \"shooter.\" Doesn't really fit that title much, but its more akin to TF2 than other games.\n-Quick rounds! Doesn't take long to play honestly which is great! Haven't played with people yet but should be a blast with friends!\n\nCons:\n-Game simply doesn't look all that nice. This helps gameplay by simplifying interactions with very little clutter and helps keep the game running smoothly on any machine, but be warned, it doesn't look any better playing than the screenshots do.\n-Poorly optimized. Even though it plays well on any machine, the game is more sluggish than a well optimized AAA game or even most indie games. Early access does mean some of this is expected.\n-No players. This might bug potential buyers more than it should because the AI isn't exactly great, but buying this game helps in this regard!\n\nAdd me if you want to play, this game is cute and cheap and frankly I think its a good example of what an amateur early access title should look like.",
